        "description": "<p>Hi HN,<p>I\u2019ve been working on esp32sim, an open-source ESP32 emulator that runs in the browser.<p>The fun part of the demo is that there is no ESP32 involved \u2014 the firmware is executing in the emulator.<p>The goal is to make ESP32 software easier to experiment with, test and simulate without always needing physical hardware connected.<p>Source:\n<a href=\"https://github.com/mikroverk/esp32sim\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/mikroverk/esp32sim</a><p>I made a short video showing it in action:\n<a href=\"https://youtu.be/waoWFilTWEc\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://youtu.be/waoWFilTWEc</a><p>I\u2019m particularly interested in feedback from embedded developers: what would an emulator like this need to support before you\u2019d actually use it for development, testing or CI?</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50131189\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50131189</a></p>\n<p>Points: 100</p>\n<p># Comments: 11</p>",
